     #S8267 Observe W2 band refactor agent (agent-a3db6377f9297d10c) delivery and OMP widget test suite refactor (W5 in progress) (Oct 13 at 8:38 PM)


     Investigated: Band refactor work: complexity reduction via helper extraction (planRows, idleRow, bandTree split); MCP tool name/target extraction
     (shortTool, targetOf); fallow audit gate validation. OMP widget: channel-view paint loop integration with renderPanel, gates cache async polling, test
     suite rewrite covering layout budgeting and collapse rules.

     Learned: Band complexity gates are satisfied by splitting functions into small helpers (each < cyclomatic 5) to stay below fallow thresholds; MCP tool
     names strip mcp__ and plugin prefixes for clean display; renderPanel delegates framing/layout/collapse logic, simplifying channel-view to a paint function
     that reads live workers, todos, notes, and gates; gates cache at 10s interval prevents blocking paint cycles (~1.5s); OMP widget tests validate proof-first
     (no fixture setup needed) across multiple widths/worker counts to ensure 10-line budget is never exceeded.

     Completed: W2 band fallow refactor: commit 067896b4 merged to main and pushed to origin. Changes include: band.tsx row planning helpers (railStep, chrome,
     tradesTicker, needsMore, etc.), short MCP tool name display via shortTool(), target extraction from file/pattern/query via targetOf(). Fallow audit passes
     (complexity_introduced=0). Plugin test suite: 277 pass, 170 fail (no new failures; 3 new tests added). W3c pane feed agent: atlas_panefeed.py module with 6
     unit tests, atlas_mux.py integration with branded inverse ATLAS header, omp/team-tool.ts with spawn/wait/reap orchestration. W5 OMP widget: channel-view
     paint loop with renderPanel and gates cache implemented; test suite refactored to proof-first validation (borders, rail, lanes, ticker, gates footer, idle
     state, collapse rules, cache throttling).

     Next Steps: W4 hook speed optimization (PEP 562 module __getattr__ lazy-load for dispatch_tripwire) remains active. W5 OMP widget test execution pending
     (bun test output truncated in prior execution; need full test run to confirm all assertions pass). W3c pane feed agent identified atlas_mux.py missing
     --output-format stream-json and --verbose flags in claude argv (test failure: test_claude_argv_and_tier_from_frontmatter expects 10 argv elements including
     stream-json flags, actual only has 6). Integration of stream-json flags into atlas_mux.py spawn logic needed to complete pane feed delivery. All parallel
     agents (W1 merged, W2 merged, W3a merged, W3c done, W4 in flight, W5 in flight) targeting Atlas 12.1.3+ redesign rollout.

     Notes: Band refactor achieves fallow clean by keeping helper functions minimal; inherited complexity from bandTree is now split across
     narrowRows/fullRows/bandColor/openChip. MCP tool display now shows actionable names (e.g., ctx_shell, ctx_read) instead of full mcp__server__tool paths.
     OMP widget renderPanel proof-first tests use plain() helper (ANSI strip) for cleaner assertions and validate layout across 40–160 width, 0–9 workers, 5–10
     line budgets. Gates cache design avoids blocking paint: async spawn via spawnText, 10s throttle, error becomes error group. W3c pane feed stream-json flag
     gap is the only identified blocker for completion; W4 and W5 progress not yet validated in this observation window.


