The dispatch was not denied. The SCOPE tripwire did not fire on an atlas:explorer call that had no SCOPE: line, so the rule from 12.2.0 ("SCOPE required on
atlas dispatches") is not being enforced on this path.

1. claude-mem search for "atlas scope gate": 15 hits. The most relevant is #38783 (plugins/atlas/scripts/atlas_scope.py, about scope determinism and
   gates_armed()).
2. Dispatch of atlas:explorer with the GOAL line and the TOOLS: ToolSearch lean-ctx (ctx_search, ctx_read) line, and no SCOPE line: the agent launched. The only
   hook output was an advisory, not a scope deny:

▎ [atlas] ADVISORY - first unbounded-dispatch offense this session, so this dispatch proceeds, but the next one is denied. Missing SUCCESS CRITERIA:, OUT OF
▎ SCOPE:, STOP CONDITIONS:, REPORT:.

That advisory is from the unbounded-dispatch check, which looks for the SUCCESS CRITERIA / OUT OF SCOPE / STOP CONDITIONS / REPORT blocks. It says nothing about
SCOPE:.

There was no deny text to quote, so I made no retry. The explorer is still running in the background, and I'll post its list of bench* files when it finishes.
One possible cause is that the scope check only runs once orchestration is armed. I haven't confirmed that. If you want to find out, the next step is to read
gates_armed() and the SCOPE branch in the dispatch tripwire.

